/P 49 0 R
/E (Similar to Bob Dylan, who unlike Kadare actually won a Nobel, they pass the artistic high bar of difficult-to-perform folk music in exchange for artistic freedom thereafter. If American folk music has a house of the rising sun to mourn for the unfulfilled life, the Albanians have the peaks where the sun sets to make way for the unrequited love. Like Bob Dylan, Sh/E unites folk purists and the cultural masses with one notable difference: they went electric from the start. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
